      "culture": "In Lebanon people ask about family early and directly, and \"خيّي\" (my brother) is also a friendly way to address a man who is not a relative. Saying you are still single (\"لسّا عازب\" for a man, \"لسّا عازبة\" for a woman) is a plain answer, and it is often met with a kind \"إن شاء الله قريب\".",
